\name{Cross-validation for the LASSO log-ratio regression with compositional response}
\alias{cv.lasso.compreg}
\title{
Cross-validation for the LASSO log-ratio regression with compositional response
}

\description{
Cross-validation for the LASSO log-ratio regression with compositional response.
}

\usage{
cv.lasso.compreg(y, x, lambda = NULL, nlambda = 100, nfolds = 10,
folds = NULL, seed = NULL)
}

\arguments{
\item{y}{
A numerical matrix with compositional data. Zero values are not allowed as the additive
log-ratio transformation is applied to the compositional response prior to implementing
the LASSO algortihm.
}
\item{x}{
A matrix with the predictor variables.
}
\item{lambda}{
A user supplied lambda sequence.
}
\item{nlambda}{
\bold{This information is copied from the package glmnet.} The number of \eqn{lambda} values,
default is 100.
}
\item{nfolds}{
The number of folds for the K-fold cross-validation, set to 10 by default.
}
\item{folds}{
If you have the list with the folds supply it here. You can also leave it NULL and it will create folds.
}
\item{seed}{
You can specify your own seed number here or leave it NULL.
}
}

\details{
The K-fold cross-validation is performed in order to select the optimal value for \eqn{\lambda}, the
penalty parameter in LASSO.
}

\value{
A list including:
\item{kld}{
The cross-validated Kullback-Leibler divergence for each value of \eqn{\lambda}.
}
\item{lambda.opt}{
The optimal value of \eqn{\lambda}.
}
\item{be}{
The regression coefficients for the optimal value of \eqn{\lambda}.
}
}

\references{
Aitchison J. (1986). The statistical analysis of compositional data. Chapman & Hall.

Friedman, J., Hastie, T. and Tibshirani, R. (2010) Regularization Paths for Generalized Linear Models via
Coordinate Descent. Journal of Statistical Software, Vol. 33(1), 1-22.
}

\author{
Michail Tsagris.

R implementation and documentation: Michail Tsagris \email{mtsagris@uoc.gr}.
}

